===Noun===
{{en-noun|p}}

# {{lb|en|finance}} The quantities representing the [[sensitivity]] of the [[price]] of [[derivative]]s to a change in underlying [[parameter]]s on which the value of an [[instrument]] or [[portfolio]] is [[dependent]] (so called because some are denoted by Greek letters).

====Hyponyms====
* {{sense|first-order measures of derivative price sensitivity}} {{l|en|delta}}, {{l|en|epsilon}}, {{l|en|lambda}} ({{l|en|elasticity}}, {{l|en|omega}}), {{l|en|rho}}, {{l|en|theta}}, {{l|en|vega}} ({{l|en|kappa}}, {{l|en|tau}})
* {{sense|second-order measures of derivative price sensitivity}} {{l|en|charm}} ({{l|en|delta decay}}, {{l|en|DdeltaDtime}}), {{l|en|gamma}}, {{l|en|vanna}} ({{l|en|DdeltaDvol}}, {{l|en|DvegaDspot}}), {{l|en|vera}} ({{l|en|rhova}}), {{l|en|veta}} ({{l|en|DvegaDtime}}), {{l|en|vomma}} ({{l|en|DvegaDvol}}, {{l|en|vega convexity}}, {{l|en|volga}}),
* {{sense|third-order measures of derivative price sensitivity}} {{l|en|color}}/{{l|en|colour}} ({{l|en|DgammaDtime}}, {{l|en|gamma decay}}), {{l|en|speed}} ({{l|en|DgammaDspot}}, {{l|en|gamma of the gamma}}), {{l|en|ultima}} ({{l|en|DvommaDvol}}), {{l|en|zomma}} ({{l|en|DgammaDvol}})
* {{sense|measures of multi-asset derivative price sensitivity}} {{l|en|correlation delta}} ({{l|en|cega}}), {{l|en|cross gamma}}, {{l|en|cross vanna}}, {{l|en|cross volga}}

